16.359.m:
Īśvara said:
Then, O great goddess, one should go to the sacred ford named Nārāyaṇa;
in its north-eastern direction lies the stepwell celebrated as Śāṇḍilya.

16.361.m:
Through the yoga of meditation, Mṛkaṇḍu [attained perfection] in a single hour, O lovely-faced lady;
right there the liṅga was installed under the name Mārkaṇḍeśvara,
which appeases all sins merely by darśana and worship.

16.362.m:
Īśvara said:
Then, O great goddess, one should go to Maṇḍūkeśvara;
the liṅga installed there is indeed named after Māṇḍūkyāyana.

16.363.m:
There are the sites and liṅgas of the eleven Rudras, O dear one,
namely Ajaikapād, Ahirbudhnya, and others by name;
one should worship them according to rule and be freed from all sins.

16.364.m:
There is the god Kandeśvara, where my matted hair was bound;
having bathed there properly, a person who worships that god
is freed from terrible sins and attains an auspicious domain.
